# Z-buffer demonstration model: two flat quads that pass through each other.
#
#   - RED  quad lies in the y = 0 plane (horizontal sheet).
#   - BLUE quad lies in the z = 0 plane (vertical sheet).
#   They intersect along the X axis, so each sheet is half in front of and half
#   behind the other.
#
# Painter's algorithm (Z-Buffer OFF): triangles are ordered by a single average
# depth, so one whole quad gets drawn over the other in the crossing region —
# the sheets look like one is simply in front of the other (WRONG).
#
# Z-buffer (Z-Buffer ON): visibility is resolved per pixel, so the sheets
# correctly interweave into a 3-D cross (CORRECT).
#
# Each quad is given as two faces with opposite winding so it stays visible from
# both sides regardless of the backface-cull setting.
mtllib zbuffer_test.mtl
o zbuffer_test

v -3.0  0.0 -3.0
v  3.0  0.0 -3.0
v  3.0  0.0  3.0
v -3.0  0.0  3.0
v -3.0 -3.0  0.0
v  3.0 -3.0  0.0
v  3.0  3.0  0.0
v -3.0  3.0  0.0

usemtl red
f 1 2 3 4
f 4 3 2 1

usemtl blue
f 5 6 7 8
f 8 7 6 5
